1
00:00:00,126 --> 00:00:02,878
Working at La Familia
wasn't part of the deal.

2
00:00:02,962 --> 00:00:05,965
Think of what you will do
in La Familia as your training,

3
00:00:06,048 --> 00:00:08,175
as your fallback for your family.

4
00:00:08,259 --> 00:00:10,052
They want to settle.

5
00:00:10,136 --> 00:00:11,679
How long will we refuse to settle?

6
00:00:11,762 --> 00:00:14,515
Their offer for damages is quite large.

7
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:17,101
Why are you talking to the victims?

8
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:19,103
You do not make decisions on your own

9
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:21,856
that can put the whole company at risk.

10
00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:26,068
If you can't respect me
in my own company, leave.

11
00:00:26,152 --> 00:00:27,153
But would you look at that.

12
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:28,863
The past has a habit of coming back.

13
00:00:28,946 --> 00:00:30,239
What do you mean?

14
00:00:30,322 --> 00:00:32,992
When you tried to pin
the blame on me for the fire.

15
00:00:33,075 --> 00:00:34,952
Is that really how you see me?

16
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,079
All I know is that you'll do anything

17
00:00:37,163 --> 00:00:40,708
and sacrifice everything
just for La Familia.

18
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,504
Pa, that's enough.

19
00:00:47,465 --> 00:00:49,467
Mm. Dear.

20
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,811
Have you seen the video?

21
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:04,148
Yes.

22
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,487
Mama accused me.

23
00:01:10,446 --> 00:01:12,323
She thinks we're behind that video.

24
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:14,116
What did I tell you?

25
00:01:14,742 --> 00:01:16,535
You shouldn't have
gone back to that place.

26
00:01:21,499 --> 00:01:24,668
Dear, we had nothing to do with that.

27
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:27,922
I know what you went through
because of that fire.

28
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:30,466
I would never do that to you.

29
00:01:32,635 --> 00:01:34,929
Your mother, of all people,
should know that.

30
00:01:35,262 --> 00:01:37,348
I know, Pa.

31
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:42,061
What I'm wondering is…

32
00:01:42,812 --> 00:01:44,647
who would do something like this?

33
00:01:47,066 --> 00:01:49,944
Did they catch the real culprit?

34
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:54,406
If they did, then why dig up the past now?

35
00:01:57,409 --> 00:01:59,829
I don't know. But, dear…

36
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:04,542
It won't do you well to dwell on it.

37
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:34,822
What do you want?

38
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,744
Who's giving you orders?

39
00:02:43,706 --> 00:02:45,332
I don't know what you're talking about.

40
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:47,543
We're the victims here.

41
00:02:57,803 --> 00:02:59,013
Are you following me?

42
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:00,681
How much are they paying you?

43
00:03:02,349 --> 00:03:03,726
I can offer more.

44
00:03:04,268 --> 00:03:08,522
If you're smart,
then you should know which side to be on.

45
00:03:09,273 --> 00:03:10,482
Why would I trust you?

46
00:03:14,737 --> 00:03:16,906
You don't have to trust me.

47
00:03:17,615 --> 00:03:18,866
In fact,

48
00:03:19,408 --> 00:03:21,035
you should be afraid of me.

49
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:24,830
Because you wouldn't want
to make an enemy out of me.

50
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:30,502
I'll give you time to think.

51
00:03:31,629 --> 00:03:33,547
Don't bother hiding.

52
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:35,549
Because I'll find you.

53
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:56,278
Sir, Ricardo won't leave me alone.

54
00:03:56,612 --> 00:03:59,698
He asked me
who's trying to block the settlement.

55
00:03:59,782 --> 00:04:01,200
What did you tell him?

56
00:04:01,283 --> 00:04:03,202
I didn't say anything, sir, but…

57
00:04:03,661 --> 00:04:05,663
this wasn't part of the deal.
This is dangerous.

58
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:06,747
I don't want to get hurt.

59
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:11,251
Here. To calm your nerves.

60
00:04:13,045 --> 00:04:14,546
Quit being paranoid.

61
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:16,632
Lie low for now.

62
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,425
Don't talk to anyone.

63
00:04:18,509 --> 00:04:19,635
Yes, sir.

64
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:21,762
This is our last conversation. Now, go.

65
00:04:44,743 --> 00:04:45,911
You again?

66
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,317
The protesters are gone.

67
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,694
I've convinced their leader to leave.

68
00:06:00,778 --> 00:06:03,155
-What about the settlement?
-I'm working on it.

69
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:05,365
I've also told the press to leave.

70
00:06:07,409 --> 00:06:08,619
-Hi, sir.
-Hi, Ms. D.

71
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:09,995
-Good morning.
-Good morning, Ms. D.

72
00:06:10,496 --> 00:06:13,373
Ms. D, any comment about the recent video?

73
00:06:13,457 --> 00:06:15,375
-What's this?
-What can you say

74
00:06:15,459 --> 00:06:18,796
about the allegation that
you're involved in the La Familia fire?

75
00:06:20,005 --> 00:06:22,925
-And you are…?
-Jonathan Martinez.

76
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:26,637
Citizen journalist.
You may have read my page, Online Exposé.

77
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:30,474
Like I've said before,
it's a baseless video.

78
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:33,977
Why don't you answer, Ms. Aragon?

79
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:37,064
The victims need answers.

80
00:06:37,147 --> 00:06:40,442
Or is it because you no longer care?

81
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:45,572
We already answered
those allegations years ago.

82
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:47,366
Have you done any research?

83
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:51,245
If you had done your job,
you would have realized

84
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:53,747
that my family was also a victim
in that tragedy.

85
00:06:53,831 --> 00:06:56,583
What was your father doing in the factory?

86
00:06:57,084 --> 00:06:58,877
If my memory serves me right,

87
00:06:58,961 --> 00:07:02,548
your own daughter gave a statement

88
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:04,842
that the fire was intentional.

89
00:07:04,925 --> 00:07:08,178
I lost my father in that fire!

90
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:11,849
Now do I still have to dignify
your accusations?

91
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:14,059
You got what you wanted.
Please escort him outside.

92
00:07:14,143 --> 00:07:15,769
-Take him outside.
-Let's go, sir.

93
00:07:15,853 --> 00:07:17,938
You can't be in here, sir. Let's go.

94
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,609
He has no right.

95
00:07:22,693 --> 00:07:24,027
No right!

96
00:07:24,695 --> 00:07:27,906
Just ignore him.
He just wanted to get a rise out of you.

97
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:29,533
I want that reporter banned.

98
00:07:29,616 --> 00:07:31,243
I want him blacklisted.

99
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:33,954
Diana, he won't be the only one
asking questions.

100
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,539
So, now more than ever,

101
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:38,333
it's important that
you and Patricia are seen together.

102
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:41,044
You need to show them a united front,

103
00:07:42,254 --> 00:07:44,506
especially since Patricia was
involved in that tragedy.

104
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,093
Have you two talked?

105
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:51,722
Is she coming back?

106
00:07:59,188 --> 00:08:00,397
Ms. D.

107
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,734
Here are the files from Finance.

108
00:08:05,277 --> 00:08:07,529
I also made a digital copy.

109
00:08:09,323 --> 00:08:11,116
Do you need me for anything else?

110
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:13,160
Yes.

111
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:15,078
You're aware of Burger City, right?

112
00:08:15,162 --> 00:08:16,914
Your partnership that fell through?

113
00:08:17,539 --> 00:08:21,627
Find out everything you can
about Burger City International,

114
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:23,629
especially the board members.

115
00:08:23,712 --> 00:08:25,339
Give me something I can use.

116
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:26,840
Find me leverage.

117
00:08:26,924 --> 00:08:29,301
La Familia needs them back.

118
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:30,552
Do you follow?

119
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:36,725
It's good that you returned to work.

120
00:08:37,142 --> 00:08:38,227
We had a deal.

121
00:08:38,644 --> 00:08:40,687
You still owe me.

122
00:08:41,355 --> 00:08:44,483
I'm not leaving until I get what I'm owed.

123
00:08:50,906 --> 00:08:53,951
Uh, Ms. D, here's the check.

124
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,374
Your first paycheck from La Familia.

125
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,877
I'll be expecting more
from you from now on.

126
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:09,758
Diana?

127
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:12,636
Can I talk to you?

128
00:09:14,846 --> 00:09:16,723
You may go back to work.

129
00:09:37,369 --> 00:09:38,912
-I'm home!
-Hi, sis.

130
00:09:38,996 --> 00:09:42,291
Patricia! Wow! You brought gifts!

131
00:09:42,374 --> 00:09:44,209
-Here.
-We have food!

132
00:09:45,669 --> 00:09:47,421
-Where do I put this?
-Finally, food!

133
00:09:47,504 --> 00:09:48,797
Just put it there.

134
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,550
April, I bought the book you needed.

135
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:53,510
Thank you, Patricia!

136
00:09:54,261 --> 00:09:55,887
I didn't forget about you, Jena.

137
00:09:55,971 --> 00:09:57,889
I got you a blouse for school.

138
00:09:57,973 --> 00:09:59,182
The color suits you.

139
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:02,185
Wow, Patricia! This is so conservative.

140
00:10:02,269 --> 00:10:04,688
Yes, so you stop wearing
those skimpy tops.

141
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:08,108
Uh, what's with all this?

142
00:10:08,191 --> 00:10:10,360
Oh, I got my first paycheck, Ma.

143
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:14,323
Pa? Pa!

144
00:10:14,406 --> 00:10:15,782
What's going on?

145
00:10:15,866 --> 00:10:18,660
-What's all this commotion?
-Pa, this is for you!

146
00:10:18,744 --> 00:10:20,037
-Wow!
-I bought you a new polo!

147
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:25,625
Hey, this looks good!
Wow, my daughter's a big shot now!

148
00:10:25,709 --> 00:10:28,086
Oh, no! I just bought these
at the flea market.

149
00:10:28,170 --> 00:10:31,465
-Your clothes are all worn out.
-Thank you.

150
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:32,883
Oh, wait.

151
00:10:32,966 --> 00:10:35,677
-I'll try it on. Wait a second.
-Sure!

152
00:10:35,761 --> 00:10:37,846
How about this? What's this?

153
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,890
-Ah, this?
-That one.

154
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:46,396
-Oh!
-Um, I bought it for myself.

155
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,731
It's my shoes for the office.

156
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:50,359
The shoes they make us use hurt my feet.

157
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:53,278
-Mm…
-What is it, Ma? Is it ugly?

158
00:10:54,613 --> 00:10:58,033
It's just that we have
so many expenses at home.

159
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:06,208
Um, I also bought you something.

160
00:11:07,209 --> 00:11:09,086
-It's a new bag.
-This is mine?

161
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:14,049
Yes. I noticed that the zipper
on the bag you use for work is broken.

162
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,467
-Patricia.
-Thank you!

163
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:17,427
-So? Do I look good?
-Wow!

164
00:11:18,804 --> 00:11:21,848
-It suits me, doesn't it?
-It does! It fits you so well!

165
00:11:21,932 --> 00:11:24,059
-It's a perfect fit.
-My Papa's so handsome!

166
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:27,062
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you so much.

167
00:11:28,522 --> 00:11:31,525
-Oh, you better eat now!
-All right, all right.

168
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:32,776
Here.

169
00:11:34,528 --> 00:11:35,654
Patricia.

170
00:11:36,655 --> 00:11:38,990
-Are you okay?
-Yes!

171
00:11:40,492 --> 00:11:41,952
But you look so tired.

172
00:11:42,035 --> 00:11:44,037
You attended work at La Familia,

173
00:11:44,121 --> 00:11:46,998
but you took up another gig, too.

174
00:11:47,082 --> 00:11:51,169
-Do you still get to sleep?
-Of course, I do.

175
00:11:51,253 --> 00:11:52,254
In the jeepney.

176
00:11:53,130 --> 00:11:54,089
Oh, I'm sorry.

177
00:11:54,172 --> 00:11:55,173
Patricia.

178
00:11:55,924 --> 00:11:57,884
If you're having a hard time
at La Familia…

179
00:11:58,593 --> 00:12:00,554
you can leave any time!

180
00:12:00,637 --> 00:12:02,389
Wait a minute, Martin.

181
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:04,891
Why are you telling Patricia to leave?

182
00:12:04,975 --> 00:12:07,060
Let her stay in the company!

183
00:12:07,144 --> 00:12:10,313
After all, we're lucky
to be doing quite well now.

184
00:12:15,986 --> 00:12:18,029
-You know, we should celebrate first.
-I told you.

185
00:12:18,113 --> 00:12:19,239
-Yes, yes.
-Come on!

186
00:12:19,322 --> 00:12:20,699
-Let's eat now.
-All right, all right.

187
00:12:20,782 --> 00:12:22,075
-Let's go!
-I told you.

188
00:12:23,243 --> 00:12:24,786
So, what are we going to do?

189
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:25,912
We sank at number two.

190
00:12:25,996 --> 00:12:28,415
We can't magic our way
to be number one again.

191
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:31,793
I want the partnership
with Burger City to push through.

192
00:12:31,877 --> 00:12:34,963
According to my sources,
their executives are currently in Manila.

193
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:40,343
Sis, do you think now's the right time?

194
00:12:41,595 --> 00:12:44,681
We're still dealing with the issue
on food poisoning.

195
00:12:45,182 --> 00:12:48,685
We're still working on
the settlement of the victims.

196
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:50,437
You think Burger City will listen to us?

197
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:55,400
People are drawing parallelisms
between the fire and the poisoning.

198
00:12:55,901 --> 00:12:58,445
Comments are mostly from social media.

199
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:02,032
But we all know public perception
can do a lot of damage.

200
00:13:02,449 --> 00:13:05,952
I believe we will reach
a settlement with the victims

201
00:13:06,036 --> 00:13:07,537
as soon as possible.

202
00:13:08,747 --> 00:13:09,998
However, you also need to know

203
00:13:10,081 --> 00:13:13,835
there's someone blocking
those talks with the victims.

204
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:16,630
There is someone who wants
to take the company down.

205
00:13:18,507 --> 00:13:19,716
Wow.

206
00:13:21,176 --> 00:13:24,429
You mean to tell me this is an inside job?

207
00:13:24,513 --> 00:13:26,723
The investigation is still ongoing,

208
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:28,725
but we'll know the result in no time.

209
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:30,310
Ongoing.

210
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:34,314
In other words,
you're giving us unconfirmed information.

211
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:36,149
Sis, come on.

212
00:13:37,025 --> 00:13:38,527
That is so unprofessional!

213
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:43,198
You're releasing unconfirmed information!

214
00:13:43,949 --> 00:13:45,033
What do you want, Ricardo?

215
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:47,702
For us to turn against each other?

216
00:13:49,538 --> 00:13:50,539
Sis.

217
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:54,334
Teddy's right.

218
00:13:54,417 --> 00:13:57,587
Why are you telling us that information?

219
00:13:58,838 --> 00:14:01,841
You better back up everything
you say, Ricardo.

220
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:04,970
And I'm warning all of you.

221
00:14:06,221 --> 00:14:10,559
I will never allow anybody
to take down La Familia.

222
00:14:11,935 --> 00:14:14,854
I assure you whoever is doing this,

223
00:14:14,938 --> 00:14:17,315
that person is going to pay.

224
00:14:23,238 --> 00:14:24,990
So, you mean, Dad,
they already know you're sabotaging

225
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:26,575
-the settlement?
-What's with you?

226
00:14:26,658 --> 00:14:27,659
Keep quiet!

227
00:14:28,535 --> 00:14:29,744
Someone might hear you.

228
00:14:31,663 --> 00:14:33,415
Well, have you talked to Carlo?

229
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:34,749
I asked him to move away.

230
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:39,129
The last time we spoke, he was
so paranoid about Ricardo following him.

231
00:14:39,588 --> 00:14:42,007
But if that Ricardo does know something…

232
00:14:42,591 --> 00:14:44,884
why hasn't he told it to Auntie?

233
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:49,264
Or do you think
they're planning something?

234
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:51,766
They're not planning anything,
and Sis doesn't know anything.

235
00:14:51,850 --> 00:14:54,185
You know how she is.
If she does know something…

236
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:56,730
she would've kicked me out
a long time ago.

237
00:14:57,856 --> 00:14:59,482
So what?

238
00:14:59,566 --> 00:15:02,569
-What do you think…
-I don't know! I don't know!

239
00:15:04,571 --> 00:15:07,365
All I know,
is I can't be kicked out of here.

240
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:12,370
No one can know what I'm doing
because I deserve La Familia.

241
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,585
Have you done any research?

242
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:22,631
If you had done your job,
you would have realized

243
00:15:22,714 --> 00:15:23,840
-that my family was also
-Ah, sir.

244
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:25,550
a victim in that tragedy.

245
00:15:26,301 --> 00:15:27,385
What's that?

246
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:30,305
Someone left this for you.

247
00:15:30,889 --> 00:15:32,390
-All right, thank you.
-Okay.

248
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:40,815
Sign one last document for me, please?

249
00:15:42,901 --> 00:15:44,235
Thank you!

250
00:15:46,863 --> 00:15:48,281
-Ms. D.
-Hm?

251
00:15:49,574 --> 00:15:52,285
Here's what you asked me
to do about Burger City.

252
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:53,370
Mm-hmm.

253
00:15:58,917 --> 00:15:59,709
Wait.

254
00:15:59,793 --> 00:16:03,088
Where's the new information
about Mr. Smith?

255
00:16:03,171 --> 00:16:05,131
I already know everything
that's written in here.

256
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:10,929
I tried to get it from
all possible sources, but…

257
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:13,056
Then you didn't try hard enough.

258
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:14,641
Mr. Smith is an important man.

259
00:16:14,724 --> 00:16:18,144
All decisions in Burger City
go through him.

260
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,480
I understand that,

261
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:23,608
that's why I checked
with all our departments,

262
00:16:23,692 --> 00:16:26,319
I read and checked all possible sources,

263
00:16:26,403 --> 00:16:27,779
and I even checked on the Internet.

264
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:30,323
-I did everything!
-I didn't ask for excuses.

265
00:16:31,366 --> 00:16:33,493
I asked for results.

266
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:38,498
You know, it may seem like
a waste of time to you.

267
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:41,334
But real success
comes from looking at the big picture,

268
00:16:41,418 --> 00:16:45,296
not just doing
the bare minimum required of you.

269
00:16:47,966 --> 00:16:50,427
I'm still on the surviving stage.

270
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:51,970
Not the success stage.

271
00:16:54,389 --> 00:16:58,476
Then we have to change that mindset.

272
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:10,405
I love my life.

273
00:17:23,752 --> 00:17:26,045
Patricia, Ms. D asked to give you this.

274
00:17:27,589 --> 00:17:28,590
Why? What's going on?

275
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:30,759
Maybe she noticed you haven't eaten yet.

276
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:33,219
-I'll get going.
-Thank you, Lara.

277
00:17:38,224 --> 00:17:39,684
It doesn't look appetizing.

278
00:18:01,247 --> 00:18:02,457
No.

279
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:05,168
We won't give in.

280
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:07,170
We're used to being hungry, right?

281
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:19,682
-You're still here, Patricia?
-Sis Tess.

282
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:21,684
Why are you still here?

283
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:24,646
Some offices want
their general cleaning today.

284
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:26,439
I still have to clean so many of them!

285
00:18:26,523 --> 00:18:28,316
I haven't even had dinner yet.

286
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:31,194
Perfect, I have a sandwich.
You can have it.

287
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:33,071
Oh, no. You have it.

288
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:34,697
Tess, just take it.

289
00:18:34,781 --> 00:18:36,658
Come on. I'm still full anyway.

290
00:18:43,081 --> 00:18:44,332
Well, I'm on a diet.

291
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,416
Fasting.

292
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:47,168
Okay. Thanks.

293
00:19:00,932 --> 00:19:02,892
Any updates on Patricia?

294
00:19:03,518 --> 00:19:04,936
She's still at her table.

295
00:19:06,104 --> 00:19:07,772
Would you like me to help her?

296
00:19:07,856 --> 00:19:09,941
Oh. No, no, no.

297
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:13,361
She needs to learn
that she has to do this on her own.

298
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:15,280
Let her swim.

299
00:19:15,363 --> 00:19:16,739
She needs to learn.

300
00:19:16,823 --> 00:19:18,533
But, Ms. D, what you're asking her to do

301
00:19:18,616 --> 00:19:19,742
-is really important.
-Enzo…

302
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:22,662
I know you can accomplish this in no time.

303
00:19:22,745 --> 00:19:24,414
You've proven yourself.

304
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:27,166
That's what I want Patricia to do, too.

305
00:19:27,834 --> 00:19:29,168
Understood, Ms. D.

306
00:20:18,676 --> 00:20:20,803
This thing is so complicated.

307
00:20:31,773 --> 00:20:33,066
Lord…

308
00:20:33,149 --> 00:20:35,109
I know you've got a lot
going on right now,

309
00:20:35,193 --> 00:20:37,111
but please, help me.

310
00:20:37,195 --> 00:20:38,363
I need coffee!

311
00:20:38,446 --> 00:20:40,531
Please tell me how to use this, Lord!

312
00:20:40,615 --> 00:20:43,201
Come on! Lord!

313
00:20:43,284 --> 00:20:44,494
Lord!

314
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:52,669
Patricia, put the beans in the grinder…

315
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:54,629
Really, Lord?

316
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:57,966
It's easy.

317
00:20:58,049 --> 00:20:59,258
Here, I'll teach you.

318
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:02,178
Get some water first.

319
00:21:03,137 --> 00:21:05,098
Just a little, okay? Don't put too much.

320
00:21:05,181 --> 00:21:06,599
Just open this top part.

321
00:21:06,683 --> 00:21:08,935
Put the water in the back.

322
00:21:10,103 --> 00:21:13,022
Okay, then turn it on to preheat.

323
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:15,149
Then grind the beans.

324
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,944
Just put in three scoops.

325
00:21:18,236 --> 00:21:19,237
Press down.

326
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:22,448
That'll be quick,
then just put it in here.

327
00:21:22,532 --> 00:21:24,158
Right here in the front. See? It's easy.

328
00:21:24,242 --> 00:21:26,035
Oh. It's actually pretty complicated!

329
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:28,413
For us, we'd just mix it from a sachet.

330
00:21:28,496 --> 00:21:31,082
That's instant coffee.
This is real coffee.

331
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:32,792
They're Sagada beans, too.

332
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:40,550
Here's your coffee, ma'am.

333
00:21:41,009 --> 00:21:42,260
About time.

334
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:45,471
It smells good.

335
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:47,515
Try it.

336
00:21:47,598 --> 00:21:48,933
They're Sagada beans.

337
00:21:49,559 --> 00:21:50,893
Mm.

338
00:22:12,457 --> 00:22:13,583
Help!

339
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:14,959
What was that?

340
00:22:20,798 --> 00:22:22,550
It's Ms. D! It's Ms. D!

341
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,641
Ms. D!

342
00:22:30,975 --> 00:22:33,227
Who are you?

343
00:22:47,992 --> 00:22:48,826
Are you okay?

344
00:22:48,910 --> 00:22:50,078
-Ms. D!
-Go after him!

345
00:22:50,161 --> 00:22:51,579
-Go after him…
-Ms. D!

346
00:22:51,662 --> 00:22:52,914
-I'm okay.
-Patricia, are you okay?

347
00:22:52,997 --> 00:22:54,082
-I'm fine. Are you?
-I'm okay.

348
00:22:54,165 --> 00:22:55,583
I'll call the police.

349
00:22:56,042 --> 00:22:58,044
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

350
00:22:58,127 --> 00:22:59,253
Security?

351
00:22:59,629 --> 00:23:00,922
We need the police here.

352
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:02,256
Call them. Hurry!

353
00:23:17,105 --> 00:23:19,107
I was having coffee with Patricia.

354
00:23:19,190 --> 00:23:21,526
When we got here,
that man was already attacking her.

355
00:23:21,609 --> 00:23:23,027
Why? What happened?

356
00:23:23,111 --> 00:23:24,862
Someone attacked Diana.

357
00:23:24,946 --> 00:23:27,115
How did that happen? Where is she?

358
00:23:27,198 --> 00:23:28,491
The medic's checking on her.

359
00:23:30,576 --> 00:23:31,577
Patricia!

360
00:23:32,328 --> 00:23:33,538
Patricia!

361
00:23:34,247 --> 00:23:35,623
Are you okay?

362
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:38,918
-Are you hurt?
-No, I'm not.

363
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:40,253
Who did this?

364
00:23:40,503 --> 00:23:41,504
Carlo Lozano.

365
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:43,673
He's the leader of the poisoning victims.

366
00:23:46,676 --> 00:23:48,469
But why would he do that?

367
00:23:48,553 --> 00:23:50,054
From the beginning, he's been the one

368
00:23:50,138 --> 00:23:52,014
who refused to cooperate
with the settlement.

369
00:23:52,098 --> 00:23:53,933
He must be really angry.

370
00:23:54,016 --> 00:23:55,560
But I have a feeling…

371
00:23:56,144 --> 00:23:57,979
someone's pulling his strings.

372
00:24:01,023 --> 00:24:02,525
Well, whoever it is…

373
00:24:03,067 --> 00:24:04,277
they need to be held accountable.

374
00:24:04,861 --> 00:24:06,612
But she was the target.

375
00:24:06,696 --> 00:24:09,031
What did she do?
Why drag other people into this?

376
00:24:09,115 --> 00:24:11,492
But how did he get in here?

377
00:24:12,034 --> 00:24:14,495
He couldn't have gotten
in here that easily.

378
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:17,039
Unless someone helped him.

379
00:24:23,754 --> 00:24:24,839
-Sir.
-Yes?

380
00:24:24,922 --> 00:24:27,341
I've already sent you
a copy of the CCTV footage.

381
00:24:27,425 --> 00:24:29,010
Okay, got it. Thank you.

382
00:24:35,558 --> 00:24:36,601
Diana.

383
00:24:37,018 --> 00:24:38,978
-Sis.
-Are you okay?

384
00:24:39,312 --> 00:24:41,480
I'm fine. You? Are you okay?

385
00:24:41,564 --> 00:24:44,233
I'm used to getting shoved around
by goons on set.

386
00:24:44,317 --> 00:24:47,278
Ms. D, the CCTV footage is ready.

387
00:25:11,344 --> 00:25:14,972
That's Carlo Lozano,
the leader of the poisoning victims.

388
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,225
Well, there you have it.

389
00:25:18,684 --> 00:25:20,436
You left the door open?

390
00:25:20,770 --> 00:25:22,355
Or did you two have an arrangement?

391
00:25:23,898 --> 00:25:25,483
I didn't let him in!

392
00:25:25,566 --> 00:25:26,734
How was I supposed to know
he was behind me?

393
00:25:26,817 --> 00:25:28,861
Stop playing dumb.
You know him, don't you?

394
00:25:28,945 --> 00:25:32,323
Didn't you two talk when you spoke
to the victims of food poisoning?

395
00:25:32,615 --> 00:25:34,825
And we all know you're angry at Diana.

396
00:25:34,909 --> 00:25:36,160
What? Did you two conspire together?

397
00:25:38,996 --> 00:25:40,581
I didn't let him in.

398
00:25:40,665 --> 00:25:42,708
You didn't let him in,
but you left the door open.

399
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:44,043
Come to think of it,

400
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:46,671
you're the only employee
who was left here.

401
00:25:46,754 --> 00:25:48,881
Maybe you were just pretending

402
00:25:48,965 --> 00:25:50,007
to work overtime so you could carry out

403
00:25:50,091 --> 00:25:52,051
whatever you were planning
with Auntie Diana.

404
00:25:52,134 --> 00:25:53,302
Wait.

405
00:25:53,844 --> 00:25:55,805
Why are you blaming my daughter?

406
00:25:55,888 --> 00:25:57,473
Blaming her? Come on.

407
00:25:57,932 --> 00:25:59,600
We all saw the video.

408
00:26:00,017 --> 00:26:01,978
I'm not blaming Patricia.

409
00:26:02,436 --> 00:26:04,480
I just noticed that ever since
she came here,

410
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:07,149
one thing after another
has gone wrong at La Familia.

411
00:26:07,233 --> 00:26:09,110
-Come on!
-That's right, Dad.

412
00:26:09,193 --> 00:26:11,487
You always make Auntie Diana
look like the bad guy.

413
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:13,823
That's right. First, when you got
kicked out of the mansion.

414
00:26:13,906 --> 00:26:15,950
Then came that video about the fire.

415
00:26:16,033 --> 00:26:18,577
-We had nothing to do with that!
-And now this!

416
00:26:18,661 --> 00:26:20,288
Before, they were just targeting
her reputation.

417
00:26:20,371 --> 00:26:22,039
Now they're targeting her directly.
Come on!

418
00:26:22,415 --> 00:26:24,166
And you immediately blame my daughter?

419
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:26,502
Well, you can't blame us
for being suspicious.

420
00:26:26,585 --> 00:26:28,713
Wherever she goes, there's trouble.

421
00:26:29,005 --> 00:26:31,048
And now Diana's life was put in danger.

422
00:26:31,132 --> 00:26:33,759
How far does your hatred
for her really go?

423
00:26:33,843 --> 00:26:35,803
Is this some kind of sick revenge?

424
00:26:37,263 --> 00:26:39,765
You know what?
That's really possible, Dad.

425
00:26:40,683 --> 00:26:43,185
Because we all know
how you treat Auntie Diana.

426
00:26:43,894 --> 00:26:46,605
She's just someone who's a boss to you.

427
00:26:46,689 --> 00:26:48,983
You always think
she's making your life difficult,

428
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:50,276
unlike us.

429
00:26:50,359 --> 00:26:53,237
Even though Auntie Diana is the boss,
at the end of the day,

430
00:26:53,571 --> 00:26:54,697
for us…

431
00:26:55,489 --> 00:26:56,991
she's still family.

432
00:26:57,908 --> 00:26:59,035
Right, Auntie?

433
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:02,705
That's enough. Just drop it.

434
00:27:03,706 --> 00:27:05,499
Let the police handle it, okay?

435
00:27:05,583 --> 00:27:07,043
They'll find out the truth.

436
00:27:09,795 --> 00:27:10,838
Let's go, dear.

437
00:27:10,921 --> 00:27:12,131
Come on.

438
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:13,758
Come on.

439
00:27:32,234 --> 00:27:33,361
Diana.

440
00:27:35,112 --> 00:27:36,113
Hmm?

441
00:27:36,614 --> 00:27:37,865
I'll give you a ride.

442
00:27:38,199 --> 00:27:40,242
It's okay. Benjie is here.

443
00:27:40,326 --> 00:27:42,328
Look, after what happened,
it's not safe for you to be alone.

444
00:27:44,246 --> 00:27:45,998
It's a good thing
I hadn't left the office yet.

445
00:27:47,458 --> 00:27:48,876
Right.

446
00:27:49,502 --> 00:27:52,338
What kept you here so late?

447
00:27:52,421 --> 00:27:54,256
I was just finishing some tasks.

448
00:27:54,340 --> 00:27:56,467
Ah. That late?

449
00:27:56,550 --> 00:27:59,428
Fortunately, my boss is a slave driver.

450
00:28:00,679 --> 00:28:01,722
You know, you should take a break.

451
00:28:04,600 --> 00:28:05,893
I can handle myself.

452
00:28:06,977 --> 00:28:09,230
Are you really like this?
Even after being attacked,

453
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:11,023
you still won't yield.

454
00:28:11,107 --> 00:28:13,943
That's exactly what the person
who did this to me wants.

455
00:28:14,026 --> 00:28:18,364
To see me affected, to see me weak.

456
00:28:18,447 --> 00:28:21,075
No, I just refuse to become a victim.

457
00:28:21,325 --> 00:28:23,869
Being vulnerable isn't weakness.

458
00:28:24,870 --> 00:28:28,082
And it won't hurt…
to admit that you need help.

459
00:28:28,874 --> 00:28:31,210
You don't have to carry it all alone.

460
00:28:32,461 --> 00:28:34,004
Good night, Ricardo.

461
00:28:52,398 --> 00:28:53,732
Who are you calling?

462
00:28:57,653 --> 00:28:59,196
None of your business.

463
00:29:00,239 --> 00:29:01,699
By the way…

464
00:29:02,616 --> 00:29:05,035
Carlo dropped this while trying to escape.

465
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:07,163
It should be easy to fix, right?

466
00:29:10,166 --> 00:29:11,292
Whoa.

467
00:29:11,917 --> 00:29:13,169
It's still working.

468
00:29:14,879 --> 00:29:16,380
You just need to power it on.

469
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:19,800
I wonder what the password could be.

470
00:29:20,217 --> 00:29:23,012
That way, I'll know
who's pulling his strings.

471
00:29:24,221 --> 00:29:25,848
Why didn't you bring that out earlier?

472
00:29:27,433 --> 00:29:29,727
I didn't know what to do with it yet.

473
00:29:31,228 --> 00:29:32,313
That depends.

474
00:29:33,981 --> 00:29:35,399
Depends?

475
00:29:35,483 --> 00:29:36,525
On what?

476
00:29:38,903 --> 00:29:40,488
I have my demands.

477
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:46,410
Are you all right?

478
00:29:46,494 --> 00:29:48,245
Looks like the blood is draining
from your face.

479
00:29:48,871 --> 00:29:50,498
Listen. Get some rest.

480
00:29:50,581 --> 00:29:51,582
Don't worry.

481
00:29:53,459 --> 00:29:55,461
I'll let you know
what I want from you soon.

482
00:30:14,021 --> 00:30:15,272
Damn you!

483
00:30:15,356 --> 00:30:18,192
You told me to wait for Diana,
to put her to sleep!

484
00:30:18,275 --> 00:30:20,194
Then why did it all blow up like that?

485
00:30:20,611 --> 00:30:22,279
I'm definitely a wanted man now!

486
00:30:24,949 --> 00:30:27,076
That's enough for you to start a new life.

487
00:30:27,159 --> 00:30:28,619
Don't ever show your face again, okay?

488
00:30:28,702 --> 00:30:30,329
If you hadn't blackmailed me…

489
00:30:30,412 --> 00:30:32,498
Carlo, this wouldn't have happened to you

490
00:30:32,581 --> 00:30:34,667
if you hadn't conspired with Teddy.

491
00:30:34,750 --> 00:30:35,834
But why?

492
00:30:35,918 --> 00:30:37,336
Why are you doing this?

493
00:30:38,379 --> 00:30:41,048
Aren't you working for Diana?
Why did you do that to her?

494
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:44,218
So that she could see me as her savior.

495
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:46,262
-By using me!
-Mmm!

496
00:30:48,389 --> 00:30:49,515
Come on now.

497
00:30:50,349 --> 00:30:52,768
I've already given you far too much.

498
00:30:53,602 --> 00:30:55,771
Isn't money all you ever wanted?

499
00:30:56,772 --> 00:30:58,482
So if I were you…

500
00:30:59,775 --> 00:31:02,111
I'd count myself lucky.

501
00:31:03,279 --> 00:31:06,198
And disappear for the rest of my life.

502
00:31:07,241 --> 00:31:09,577
Because if you ever come back…

503
00:31:11,036 --> 00:31:12,204
…you will regret it.

504
00:31:12,580 --> 00:31:14,873
You have no idea
what I'm capable of doing to you.

505
00:31:38,772 --> 00:31:40,482
-You still want more, right?
-Exactly!

506
00:31:40,566 --> 00:31:41,817
-Hey, buy some snacks!
-Thanks, but no thanks.

507
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:44,361
-Come on, it's only cheap!
-Is it really good?

508
00:31:44,445 --> 00:31:46,739
-Wait a sec. Patricia.
-It tastes like heaven.

509
00:31:46,822 --> 00:31:48,824
Is it true that something
happened here last night?

510
00:31:48,907 --> 00:31:50,200
We heard there was an intruder.

511
00:31:50,284 --> 00:31:51,493
Can you confirm?

512
00:31:51,869 --> 00:31:53,746
Look, Harvey…

513
00:31:54,163 --> 00:31:56,540
I'm peddling baked stuffed buns,
not rumors.

514
00:31:56,624 --> 00:31:58,042
-Just asking a question.
-You're rubbing off on me.

515
00:31:58,125 --> 00:32:00,336
Hey, maybe someone in your family
has a birthday coming up.

516
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:02,463
-My sibling.
-Wait, really? Contact me.

517
00:32:02,546 --> 00:32:03,672
-Okay.
-I take bulk orders.

518
00:32:03,756 --> 00:32:06,133
For weddings, wakes, baptisms.

519
00:32:06,216 --> 00:32:08,052
-Delicious, right?
-Totally.

520
00:32:08,135 --> 00:32:10,054
How about a snack
to bring to your table? Hang on.

521
00:32:10,137 --> 00:32:11,138
-You're good.
-So yummy.

522
00:32:11,221 --> 00:32:12,598
I know, right? So buy some more!

523
00:32:12,681 --> 00:32:14,600
-Patricia.
-Enzo, would you like to buy some?

524
00:32:14,975 --> 00:32:16,268
Ms. D is calling for you.

525
00:32:16,685 --> 00:32:18,145
Sure. I'll just finish this.

526
00:32:18,437 --> 00:32:19,730
Actually…

527
00:32:21,482 --> 00:32:23,484
it's the exact reason
she wants you in her office.

528
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:27,821
She's heard about your side hustle.

529
00:32:29,448 --> 00:32:30,574
And she's not pleased.

530
00:32:30,866 --> 00:32:31,992
Uh-oh.

531
00:32:50,844 --> 00:32:52,137
Uh…

532
00:32:53,138 --> 00:32:55,516
Any updates from the police?

533
00:32:56,225 --> 00:32:57,726
I'm fine.

534
00:33:03,357 --> 00:33:05,651
Do you want a baked stuffed bun?

535
00:33:08,779 --> 00:33:10,072
As part of the deal we agreed on.

536
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:17,621
Nice. Just eight to go then.

537
00:33:17,996 --> 00:33:19,790
Aren't you earning enough?

538
00:33:19,873 --> 00:33:21,250
You're still taking small roles, right?

539
00:33:21,792 --> 00:33:24,128
Expenses never end.

540
00:33:24,378 --> 00:33:27,297
And this is just a small business.

541
00:33:27,589 --> 00:33:29,425
Still honest work.

542
00:33:29,508 --> 00:33:31,051
Clean money.

543
00:33:31,468 --> 00:33:33,220
Want one? There's a little left.

544
00:33:33,303 --> 00:33:35,264
Do you really need money that badly?

545
00:33:38,475 --> 00:33:41,770
I've long accepted that
I can only rely on myself.

546
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:45,983
Because I know what it feels like
to have nothing

547
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:48,402
and no one to help.

548
00:33:48,485 --> 00:33:52,322
Why don't you just give me
the full amount we agreed on?

549
00:33:52,406 --> 00:33:54,032
Seems like you don't want me here anyway.

550
00:33:54,116 --> 00:33:56,869
Who told you that I don't want you here?

551
00:33:58,620 --> 00:34:01,832
What's your plan
once you've got the rest of it?

552
00:34:04,334 --> 00:34:06,170
I'll use it to pay off our debts.

553
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:08,130
Once that's done,

554
00:34:08,213 --> 00:34:11,008
I can finally do what I've always wanted.

555
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:14,970
To become a famous actress.

556
00:34:16,680 --> 00:34:18,766
And when that day comes…

557
00:34:19,683 --> 00:34:22,102
I like it to be because I worked for it.

558
00:34:22,978 --> 00:34:24,980
Because I gave it my all.

559
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:31,361
Not just because I'm an Aragon.

560
00:34:33,447 --> 00:34:35,282
Anything else you want me to do?

561
00:34:51,048 --> 00:34:52,549
I made that myself.

562
00:35:16,240 --> 00:35:18,617
Uh… please listen, everyone.

563
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:20,369
Wait a second.

564
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:22,538
Because of what happened to Carlo…

565
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:28,377
we decided to talk to you as a group.

566
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:30,671
We're willing to make a settlement.

567
00:35:30,754 --> 00:35:32,589
But we have a request.

568
00:35:32,965 --> 00:35:33,966
What is it?

569
00:35:34,049 --> 00:35:36,885
We want to talk to someone
who will really listen.

570
00:35:36,969 --> 00:35:38,512
-That's right.
-Yes.

571
00:35:38,595 --> 00:35:39,680
Someone who'll listen.

572
00:35:39,763 --> 00:35:42,808
Do you have anyone in mind?

573
00:35:42,891 --> 00:35:44,560
The one who talked to Elsa.

574
00:35:44,643 --> 00:35:45,727
The girl who saved her son's life.

575
00:35:45,811 --> 00:35:48,021
-That's right.
-Right?

576
00:35:49,231 --> 00:35:50,983
Right? You agree, right?

577
00:35:55,779 --> 00:35:58,782
You! Did you think I wouldn't find out
you stole from me?

578
00:35:58,866 --> 00:36:00,409
-Ma'am, no!
-Admit it!

579
00:36:00,492 --> 00:36:02,244
-My money's all gone!
-Ma'am, I didn't do it!

580
00:36:02,327 --> 00:36:04,288
-You thought I wouldn't know?
-Ma'am, no!

581
00:36:04,371 --> 00:36:05,914
-Look at me!
-I didn't steal anything!

582
00:36:05,998 --> 00:36:07,374
What? You're a liar!

583
00:36:07,457 --> 00:36:09,001
-No…
-Cut!

584
00:36:09,084 --> 00:36:10,085
Okay, come here.

585
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:12,129
-Patricia, you were so good.
-How are you?

586
00:36:12,212 --> 00:36:13,213
-Are you okay?
-You're giving everything

587
00:36:13,297 --> 00:36:14,172
even in practice.

588
00:36:14,256 --> 00:36:15,132
Thank you.

589
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:16,884
-Andi, just do it like that.
-Okay, Director.

590
00:36:16,967 --> 00:36:18,385
-Thank you.
-Okay. You can stand here.

591
00:36:18,468 --> 00:36:20,387
Kaori, do the same thing.

592
00:36:20,470 --> 00:36:22,848
-Andi…
-That hurts.

593
00:36:22,931 --> 00:36:24,516
Hey. You were really
crying so hard there, bestie.

594
00:36:24,600 --> 00:36:25,809
You did better than the actress.

595
00:36:25,893 --> 00:36:27,686
Oh. Shh. They might hear you.

596
00:36:27,769 --> 00:36:29,938
I did my best
to gain the director's favor.

597
00:36:30,439 --> 00:36:33,150
I know that
we really want to be recognized.

598
00:36:33,233 --> 00:36:34,860
But you're working so hard.

599
00:36:34,943 --> 00:36:36,236
Are you trying to prove something?

600
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:37,487
Yes.

601
00:36:37,571 --> 00:36:38,906
What?

602
00:36:40,824 --> 00:36:42,618
That I can survive on my own.

603
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:45,787
That I'm going to be a lead
and I'm going to be famous.

604
00:36:45,871 --> 00:36:47,497
All my dreams will come true.

605
00:36:49,249 --> 00:36:50,375
Let me guess.

606
00:36:51,001 --> 00:36:52,169
It's because of your mom, isn't it?

607
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:55,297
Yes.

608
00:36:56,048 --> 00:36:59,259
I don't want to feel
like I need anything from her.

609
00:37:01,553 --> 00:37:04,348
So I really hope I can
bag a lead role soon, bestie.

610
00:37:05,098 --> 00:37:07,935
I want to show her
that I don't need her surname.

611
00:37:08,018 --> 00:37:09,394
Just remember, bestie.

612
00:37:09,478 --> 00:37:11,313
Include me in your plans, okay?

613
00:37:11,396 --> 00:37:12,522
Of course.

614
00:37:27,996 --> 00:37:29,247
Ouch.

615
00:37:29,998 --> 00:37:32,042
-Patricia.
-Yes? Oh.

616
00:37:32,125 --> 00:37:33,293
Good morning.

617
00:37:33,752 --> 00:37:35,003
Do you need anything?

618
00:37:35,087 --> 00:37:36,213
Yes.

619
00:37:36,296 --> 00:37:37,714
What happened to your face?

620
00:37:39,466 --> 00:37:40,676
Oh.

621
00:37:40,759 --> 00:37:43,595
It's nothing.
I just tried a new skincare product.

622
00:37:44,972 --> 00:37:46,348
What do you need?

623
00:37:46,932 --> 00:37:52,437
The victims requested you to talk to them
for settlement negotiations.

624
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:54,564
Me? Why me?

625
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:57,776
They warmed up to you
when you talked to them.

626
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:01,697
Maybe they were impressed by your courage.

627
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,825
And I think
you're the only one they trust.

628
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:10,539
The poisoning victims agreed
to sign the agreement.

629
00:38:10,622 --> 00:38:12,207
-Oh.
-Oh. That's good.

630
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:14,501
That's good.

631
00:38:16,169 --> 00:38:18,839
I heard that Patricia
has been a great help

632
00:38:18,922 --> 00:38:20,757
in convincing the victims.

633
00:38:21,425 --> 00:38:25,679
Looks like you've already taken her
under your wing, Diana.

634
00:38:26,179 --> 00:38:31,393
Does this mean that nothing will stop us
from pursuing Burger City?

635
00:38:31,476 --> 00:38:32,978
You know how big

636
00:38:33,061 --> 00:38:34,896
this deal is for La Familia.

637
00:38:34,980 --> 00:38:37,274
Yes. I'm working on it.

638
00:38:37,607 --> 00:38:39,234
-Good.
-I'm sorry, Sis.

639
00:38:39,651 --> 00:38:41,695
It seems we're not out of the woods yet.

640
00:38:42,738 --> 00:38:44,239
What do you mean?

641
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:47,325
Uh, have you seen this?

642
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:55,208
Based on the documents I have,

643
00:38:55,584 --> 00:38:58,378
La Familia was on the brink
of bankruptcy for a long time

644
00:38:58,462 --> 00:39:00,922
before the fire happened.

645
00:39:01,381 --> 00:39:03,759
Declining revenues,

646
00:39:04,134 --> 00:39:05,594
mounting debt,

647
00:39:05,677 --> 00:39:08,430
failed expansion projects.

648
00:39:08,513 --> 00:39:11,475
They almost declared bankruptcy.

649
00:39:12,059 --> 00:39:15,562
Was the fire their solution?

650
00:39:15,937 --> 00:39:19,858
Was the factory fire a desperate attempt

651
00:39:19,941 --> 00:39:22,069
at saving the company?

652
00:39:24,863 --> 00:39:27,115
Where did he get those papers?

653
00:39:27,866 --> 00:39:29,076
I'll try to find out.

654
00:39:29,826 --> 00:39:31,953
You better do it now.

655
00:39:53,225 --> 00:39:54,476
Ms. D.

656
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:57,104
Where's your dad?

657
00:40:18,250 --> 00:40:20,418
Are you waiting for my boyfriend?

658
00:40:20,669 --> 00:40:22,796
Sorry, I'm here, not him.

659
00:40:23,463 --> 00:40:24,339
How dare…

660
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:25,882
Cut!

661
00:40:25,966 --> 00:40:28,093
My god. What happened?

662
00:40:28,176 --> 00:40:30,512
That's not part of the scene.

663
00:40:31,138 --> 00:40:33,265
Director, I'm sorry.
I was caught up in my emotions.

664
00:40:33,348 --> 00:40:35,600
-Kaori…
-But it turned out good.

665
00:40:36,268 --> 00:40:37,394
Fine, go over there.

666
00:40:37,477 --> 00:40:38,603
Next setup!

667
00:40:38,687 --> 00:40:39,896
-Yes, Director.
-Are you okay?

668
00:40:39,980 --> 00:40:41,606
-Yes. I'm okay.
-Are you sure?

669
00:40:41,690 --> 00:40:43,066
Yes, don't worry about it.

670
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:45,318
You know, I know a producer

671
00:40:45,402 --> 00:40:47,404
who's planning to produce an indie film.

672
00:40:47,904 --> 00:40:51,658
That film will be screened
at international film festivals abroad.

673
00:40:52,159 --> 00:40:53,869
I think you're fit for the lead role.

674
00:40:53,952 --> 00:40:54,953
Lead role.

675
00:40:55,036 --> 00:40:58,957
Yes. Someone vulnerable but brave.

676
00:40:59,624 --> 00:41:02,544
Someone with a soft heart
but… is also fierce.

677
00:41:02,627 --> 00:41:04,129
Just like that.

678
00:41:04,212 --> 00:41:06,214
And someone who is willing to do anything.

679
00:41:06,506 --> 00:41:08,633
Oh! That's me!

680
00:41:08,717 --> 00:41:10,093
Would you like to audition later?

681
00:41:10,177 --> 00:41:11,428
I would love to.

682
00:41:11,511 --> 00:41:13,138
Okay, that's just
for the sake of formality.

683
00:41:13,221 --> 00:41:15,557
But I'm going to recommend you, okay?

684
00:41:15,974 --> 00:41:17,684
But they only have a small budget

685
00:41:17,767 --> 00:41:19,269
because it's indie.

686
00:41:19,936 --> 00:41:21,897
And we have to start filming
as soon as possible,

687
00:41:21,980 --> 00:41:23,815
so we need to find a lead.

688
00:41:23,899 --> 00:41:24,900
Are you okay with that?

689
00:41:24,983 --> 00:41:26,943
Yes. No problem. I would love to do it.

690
00:41:27,402 --> 00:41:28,945
Okay. I'll message you the details later.

691
00:41:29,029 --> 00:41:30,822
-Okay, Director. Thank you.
-Okay.

692
00:41:31,323 --> 00:41:33,116
-Next setup!
-Bestie!

693
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:34,659
-Wipe yourself dry.
-Oh.

694
00:41:34,743 --> 00:41:36,453
-You're drenched.
-Thank you.

695
00:41:36,536 --> 00:41:39,706
-What was that?
-I'm going to be a lead!

696
00:41:39,789 --> 00:41:40,749
Oh, wow!

697
00:41:41,416 --> 00:41:44,085
I think this is the beginning
of my road to stardom.

698
00:41:44,544 --> 00:41:47,130
When it happens, you already know it.

699
00:41:47,214 --> 00:41:50,258
-What do I know?
-I'll be able to free myself from my mom.

700
00:41:50,342 --> 00:41:52,636
-Mm…
-I don't have to take

701
00:41:52,719 --> 00:41:54,512
the money she's paying me.

702
00:41:54,596 --> 00:41:57,349
Because I'll be able to earn that amount

703
00:41:57,432 --> 00:42:00,018
and more once I become famous.

704
00:42:00,894 --> 00:42:03,521
Patricia Dela Cruz. Superstar.

705
00:42:11,655 --> 00:42:14,991
I've read all the articles about him.

706
00:42:15,075 --> 00:42:17,285
I've seen all the pictures too.

707
00:42:17,369 --> 00:42:19,996
And this? This freaking resume!

708
00:42:20,622 --> 00:42:22,040
If this is all you have for me,

709
00:42:22,123 --> 00:42:23,416
I might as well have asked
our HR department.

710
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,252
Those are the initial materials
I was able to dig up…

711
00:42:25,335 --> 00:42:26,503
Initial?

712
00:42:26,586 --> 00:42:28,171
So, I should expect more?

713
00:42:28,713 --> 00:42:31,132
Come on, I want what I don't already know.

714
00:42:31,216 --> 00:42:34,302
Anything on Ricardo Salvador
that could take him down.

715
00:42:35,178 --> 00:42:37,347
Everyone has skeletons in their closet.

716
00:42:37,430 --> 00:42:40,058
That's what I need to know.

717
00:42:40,141 --> 00:42:41,393
Not this!

718
00:42:42,811 --> 00:42:45,605
-Go.
-Okay, sir. Excuse me.

719
00:42:55,657 --> 00:42:56,866
Patricia!

720
00:42:57,784 --> 00:42:59,577
-Sir Victor?
-Yes, that's me.

721
00:43:00,287 --> 00:43:01,997
-My gosh.
-How have you been?

722
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:03,748
I've been well.

723
00:43:03,832 --> 00:43:04,916
Long time no see.

724
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:07,127
We worked together
on The Two Faces of Eve, right?

725
00:43:07,210 --> 00:43:10,422
-That's right. It was fun.
-I'm glad you remember me.

726
00:43:10,505 --> 00:43:13,383
-Of course. You look slimmer.
-Oh, thank you.

727
00:43:13,466 --> 00:43:15,218
-I'm really glad you still remember me.
-Yes.

728
00:43:15,302 --> 00:43:16,428
Have you eaten?

729
00:43:16,511 --> 00:43:18,722
I'm good. Are you part of this film too?

730
00:43:18,805 --> 00:43:21,808
-Yes, I'm the producer.
-Wow.

731
00:43:21,891 --> 00:43:24,144
I'm also the co-director.

732
00:43:24,227 --> 00:43:26,771
So, join me and have a seat.

733
00:43:27,188 --> 00:43:29,149
Uh, waiter?

734
00:43:29,816 --> 00:43:31,943
Go ahead and order.
They’re still setting up upstairs.

735
00:43:32,027 --> 00:43:33,361
-Oh, okay.
-Yes.

736
00:43:33,445 --> 00:43:35,113
-What should I get?
-Anything.

737
00:43:35,196 --> 00:43:39,701
Uh… I'll just get
iced coffee with milk, please.

738
00:43:40,076 --> 00:43:41,119
Thank you.

739
00:43:41,703 --> 00:43:44,414
-How have you been?
-I'm an office worker now.

740
00:43:44,497 --> 00:43:45,498
-Really?
-Yes.

741
00:43:45,582 --> 00:43:46,583
How's work?

742
00:43:46,666 --> 00:43:49,085
It's all right. I’ve been pretty busy,

743
00:43:49,169 --> 00:43:51,171
but I'm still selling toasted steamed bun.

744
00:43:51,254 --> 00:43:54,132
-Wow.
-Would you like to buy some?

745
00:43:54,507 --> 00:43:56,968
All right, I'll buy some later.

746
00:43:57,886 --> 00:43:59,804
-Where's the director, by the way?
-He's on his way.

747
00:43:59,888 --> 00:44:01,264
-Ah, okay.
-He's just running a bit late.

748
00:44:01,348 --> 00:44:02,974
I need to use the restroom.

749
00:44:03,058 --> 00:44:04,726
Oh, it's over there.
Just keep walking straight.

750
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:06,144
-Okay. Thank you.
-Okay.

751
00:44:16,279 --> 00:44:18,365
Just put it here, please.

752
00:44:21,368 --> 00:44:22,452
Thank you.

753
00:44:51,022 --> 00:44:52,982
-Your order's here.
-Thank you.

754
00:44:53,066 --> 00:44:56,027
So, what are the details
of the character I'm playing?

755
00:44:56,111 --> 00:44:57,195
-I want to internalize it.
-Ah.

756
00:44:57,278 --> 00:44:59,155
You have a good character here.

757
00:44:59,239 --> 00:45:00,782
Very challenging.

758
00:45:00,865 --> 00:45:02,826
But I'll give you the details later.

759
00:45:02,909 --> 00:45:03,952
Just relax for now.

760
00:45:04,035 --> 00:45:05,620
Go on and try your order.

761
00:45:06,329 --> 00:45:08,039
-Is that coffee?
-Yes.

762
00:45:10,792 --> 00:45:11,835
Mm.

763
00:45:17,382 --> 00:45:18,425
Yes, ma'am?

764
00:45:18,508 --> 00:45:20,301
I'd like to renew my business permit.

765
00:45:20,385 --> 00:45:22,345
How long does it usually take?

766
00:45:22,429 --> 00:45:25,849
Around two to three days.

767
00:45:25,932 --> 00:45:28,643
Because we're getting a lot
of renewal requests right now.

768
00:45:28,726 --> 00:45:30,186
I really need it ASAP.

769
00:45:30,270 --> 00:45:31,563
This is the only free time I have.

770
00:45:31,646 --> 00:45:35,400
Sorry, but there are
a lot of people lined up.

771
00:45:35,483 --> 00:45:37,986
Maybe we could work something out.

772
00:45:38,069 --> 00:45:40,488
Well… I suppose we could find a way.

773
00:45:42,782 --> 00:45:44,117
What is this?

774
00:45:44,492 --> 00:45:46,494
I really need it urgently.

775
00:45:47,162 --> 00:45:49,289
Well, for this…

776
00:45:49,372 --> 00:45:52,292
the process is very fast.

777
00:45:52,375 --> 00:45:54,586
Don't worry. I'll take care of it.

778
00:45:54,878 --> 00:45:56,337
Her name is Patricia.

779
00:45:56,421 --> 00:45:58,131
She'll be your partner.

780
00:45:58,214 --> 00:45:59,757
-This is Jaymark.
-I'm Jaymark.

781
00:45:59,841 --> 00:46:01,342
-I'm Patricia.
-Hey.

782
00:46:01,426 --> 00:46:02,635
Are you okay?

783
00:46:03,261 --> 00:46:04,262
Hey.

784
00:46:04,345 --> 00:46:06,014
I think I'm just nervous.

785
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,390
This is my first time playing the lead.

786
00:46:07,474 --> 00:46:08,808
Where's the director?

787
00:46:08,892 --> 00:46:10,727
Uh… he's just running late.

788
00:46:10,810 --> 00:46:12,520
Why are you just using a cellphone?

789
00:46:12,604 --> 00:46:14,939
That's how indie films
are made these days.

790
00:46:15,023 --> 00:46:17,901
This is a love story,
so people will surely like it.

791
00:46:17,984 --> 00:46:19,944
You two can come up with your own lines.

792
00:46:20,028 --> 00:46:21,321
Huh? Why?

793
00:46:21,404 --> 00:46:23,364
Improv's popular these days.

794
00:46:23,448 --> 00:46:24,574
Your character's name is Cindy.

795
00:46:24,657 --> 00:46:26,493
You're upset with your boyfriend.

796
00:46:26,576 --> 00:46:28,369
He comes over to win you back.

797
00:46:28,453 --> 00:46:30,747
And after that, you'll make up with him.

798
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:33,249
You'll show him how much you love him.

799
00:46:33,333 --> 00:46:36,044
-Can you do that?
-How am I supposed to show…

800
00:46:36,127 --> 00:46:38,046
He'll take care of it.

801
00:46:38,129 --> 00:46:39,255
-Right?
-Yes.

802
00:46:39,339 --> 00:46:40,548
Now go over there.

803
00:46:40,632 --> 00:46:43,218
You can do this, Patricia.
You can do this.

804
00:46:43,593 --> 00:46:45,845
Five, four, three, two… Action!

805
00:46:46,346 --> 00:46:47,347
Babe.

806
00:46:48,765 --> 00:46:51,267
-Babe…
-You cheated on me!

807
00:46:54,687 --> 00:46:56,314
I don't love her.

808
00:46:56,397 --> 00:46:58,274
You know you're the only one I love.

809
00:46:59,943 --> 00:47:01,069
What?

810
00:47:03,238 --> 00:47:04,280
Get away from me!

811
00:47:04,364 --> 00:47:06,282
Babe, let's talk.

812
00:47:06,741 --> 00:47:09,244
-Stay there!
-Hey, listen to me first.

813
00:47:09,577 --> 00:47:11,955
I'm sick of this! Let's break up!

814
00:47:13,081 --> 00:47:16,376
Babe, what can I do
to get you to forgive me?

815
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:24,175
I'll do anything to prove
how much I love you.

816
00:47:29,722 --> 00:47:31,683
-Babe…
-Wait, wait…

817
00:47:33,643 --> 00:47:35,270
I'll take care of you.

818
00:47:38,523 --> 00:47:39,649
No! Wait!

819
00:47:39,732 --> 00:47:41,317
Wait, just a second.

820
00:47:41,401 --> 00:47:43,111
-Cut. Cut. Cut.
-No. Keep going.

821
00:47:43,194 --> 00:47:44,362
You want to be famous, right?

822
00:47:44,445 --> 00:47:45,822
-Then just bear it.
-Relax.

823
00:47:45,905 --> 00:47:47,991
What? Wait. This wasn't part of the deal!

824
00:47:48,074 --> 00:47:49,284
-Stop it!
-Babe…

825
00:47:56,416 --> 00:47:57,584
Director!

826
00:47:57,667 --> 00:47:58,960
Oh, come on! Keep going!

827
00:47:59,043 --> 00:48:00,837
-But it's gross!
-Just do it!

828
00:48:03,631 --> 00:48:05,008
-Babe…
-No…

829
00:48:05,091 --> 00:48:06,342
Stop…

830
00:48:06,843 --> 00:48:08,094
I said stop!

831
00:48:12,724 --> 00:48:13,725
Get her!

832
00:48:14,058 --> 00:48:16,477
-It hurts!
-She closed the door!

833
00:48:18,396 --> 00:48:19,814
Patricia, open the door!

834
00:48:20,523 --> 00:48:21,649
Open the door!

835
00:48:29,198 --> 00:48:30,366
Hello, Patricia?

836
00:48:30,450 --> 00:48:31,784
Enzo, help me. Please…

837
00:48:32,535 --> 00:48:34,037
What's wrong? Where are you?

838
00:48:34,120 --> 00:48:35,955
Help me. I'm at the Meridian Hotel.

839
00:48:36,039 --> 00:48:37,081
I'm in room…

840
00:48:37,165 --> 00:48:38,583
-Hello, Enzo?
-Hey!

841
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:40,209
-Enzo?
-Patricia?

842
00:48:41,002 --> 00:48:42,879
-Patricia!
-Hello, Enzo!

843
00:48:46,674 --> 00:48:48,968
Ms. D! Ms. D!

844
00:48:51,846 --> 00:48:53,306
I said open the door!

845
00:48:53,389 --> 00:48:54,891
Just leave me alone!

846
00:48:54,974 --> 00:48:56,351
Come out.

847
00:48:56,434 --> 00:48:58,102
Let's just talk!

848
00:48:58,186 --> 00:48:59,646
This is just a misunderstanding.

849
00:48:59,729 --> 00:49:01,606
Come out. Let's talk.

850
00:49:01,689 --> 00:49:03,566
-Come on…
-Don't lie, you pervert!

851
00:49:03,650 --> 00:49:04,942
You're making him rape me!

852
00:49:05,026 --> 00:49:06,235
Carlota!

853
00:49:06,986 --> 00:49:09,614
Oh. Yes, sir?

854
00:49:09,697 --> 00:49:12,408
I heard you've been taking bribes.

855
00:49:12,492 --> 00:49:14,911
Sir, are you sure that it's me,

856
00:49:14,994 --> 00:49:17,413
because there's no way I would do that.

857
00:49:17,497 --> 00:49:19,499
There have been suspicions of you

858
00:49:19,582 --> 00:49:21,709
doing some illegal activities
in the office.

859
00:49:21,793 --> 00:49:23,711
Don't deny it, because…

860
00:49:26,297 --> 00:49:27,840
Ah, sir…

861
00:49:27,924 --> 00:49:31,177
Madam was asking for help a while ago…

862
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:34,180
-I was just helping…
-I'm sorry, Carlota.

863
00:49:36,391 --> 00:49:39,352
Miss, I want to know where my daughter is.

864
00:49:39,435 --> 00:49:40,895
The room number, ma'am?

865
00:49:40,978 --> 00:49:43,523
We got a call from her asking for help.

866
00:49:43,606 --> 00:49:44,899
We need your help!

867
00:49:44,982 --> 00:49:46,609
Did she tell you who she was with?

868
00:49:46,693 --> 00:49:48,486
She didn't mention, Ms. D.

869
00:49:48,569 --> 00:49:50,029
Hurry, please!

870
00:49:51,030 --> 00:49:52,323
My god, you're wasting my time!

871
00:49:52,407 --> 00:49:53,991
Let me see your CCTV. Come on.

872
00:49:54,075 --> 00:49:57,412
Uh, we don't give CCTV access
to anyone, ma'am.

873
00:49:57,495 --> 00:49:59,789
It's our protocol for the guests' privacy.

874
00:49:59,872 --> 00:50:02,667
Protocol? We're trying to save
my daughter's life here!

875
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:03,835
Which is more important?

876
00:50:03,918 --> 00:50:05,461
Your protocol or my daughter's safety?

877
00:50:05,545 --> 00:50:08,756
I'm telling you,
if something happens to her,

878
00:50:08,840 --> 00:50:10,758
I'll make you all pay!

879
00:50:11,300 --> 00:50:13,428
She won't come out, huh.

880
00:50:16,931 --> 00:50:18,391
Well, if you don't want to go out…

881
00:50:20,351 --> 00:50:22,562
I'm coming in myself.

882
00:50:26,816 --> 00:50:28,651
-Let me go!
-You thought I couldn't make it in?

883
00:50:28,735 --> 00:50:29,986
-Let me go!
-What now?

884
00:50:31,738 --> 00:50:32,864
Do it!

885
00:50:32,947 --> 00:50:35,825
Please… I'm begging you.

886
00:50:35,908 --> 00:50:36,993
Please don't do this.

887
00:50:37,076 --> 00:50:38,286
I know you're a good person.

888
00:50:38,369 --> 00:50:41,205
-You don't have to do this.
-I'm sorry. I have to do this.

889
00:50:42,123 --> 00:50:43,166
Stop…

890
00:50:47,128 --> 00:50:48,129
Help…

891
00:50:48,796 --> 00:50:49,630
Help!

892
00:50:55,678 --> 00:50:57,722
Where's my daughter? Patricia!

893
00:50:57,805 --> 00:50:58,806
What is it?

894
00:50:58,890 --> 00:51:00,600
What's going on here?

895
00:51:00,683 --> 00:51:01,809
I'm the director.

896
00:51:01,893 --> 00:51:03,436
What did you do to Patricia?

897
00:51:03,519 --> 00:51:05,146
We had an agreement.

898
00:51:05,229 --> 00:51:07,607
She wanted a lead role,
and that's why she's here.

899
00:51:09,233 --> 00:51:10,485
Help me!

900
00:51:10,568 --> 00:51:11,778
What do you care?

901
00:51:11,861 --> 00:51:13,696
Well, I'm her mother!

902
00:51:13,780 --> 00:51:17,158
She called us earlier asking for help.

903
00:51:17,241 --> 00:51:18,242
Don't be too loud.

904
00:51:19,744 --> 00:51:21,412
Where is my daughter?

905
00:51:21,496 --> 00:51:23,206
What are you talking about?

906
00:51:24,415 --> 00:51:25,792
Help!

907
00:51:25,875 --> 00:51:27,293
-Patricia!
-Patricia!

908
00:51:27,919 --> 00:51:29,295
Stop!

909
00:51:31,631 --> 00:51:33,382
Keep her quiet!

910
00:51:42,183 --> 00:51:43,893
Stop it! Give me that!

911
00:51:43,976 --> 00:51:45,394
Give me that!

912
00:51:46,562 --> 00:51:47,688
I got it.

913
00:51:48,314 --> 00:51:50,066
-Keep quiet!
-Patricia!

914
00:51:51,234 --> 00:51:54,862
Hey! What are you doing to my daughter?

915
00:51:54,946 --> 00:51:56,364
Get off her!

916
00:51:56,447 --> 00:51:57,782
You bastard!

917
00:51:57,865 --> 00:51:58,783
You're a liar!

918
00:51:59,534 --> 00:52:02,119
-Ms. D. Ms. D.
-You monster!

919
00:52:06,541 --> 00:52:08,835
-Stop it! Enzo!
-Hey!

920
00:52:22,890 --> 00:52:24,642
Enzo! Enzo!

921
00:52:24,725 --> 00:52:26,686
Enzo… Enzo. Enzo!

922
00:52:28,688 --> 00:52:30,064
You bastard!

923
00:52:30,147 --> 00:52:31,732
What were you doing to my daughter?

924
00:52:31,816 --> 00:52:33,609
-Huh?
-I'm just following directions!

925
00:52:33,693 --> 00:52:35,778
Do you think I'll believe that?

926
00:52:35,862 --> 00:52:38,656
I'm telling the truth, ma'am.
I owe them a lot of money.

927
00:52:38,906 --> 00:52:40,449
They said I can pay with this.

928
00:52:41,284 --> 00:52:43,369
You monsters!

929
00:52:43,452 --> 00:52:45,413
Stay there! Stay there!

930
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:50,334
Arrest those bastards!

931
00:52:51,043 --> 00:52:52,336
Patricia…

932
00:52:53,462 --> 00:52:55,965
Are you okay? Dear?

933
00:52:58,593 --> 00:52:59,677
Patricia!

934
00:53:02,096 --> 00:53:05,266
Make sure you do a thorough investigation.

935
00:53:05,349 --> 00:53:06,893
-Yes, ma'am.
-It's an important case.

936
00:53:06,976 --> 00:53:08,728
-Copy, ma'am.
-Thank you.

937
00:53:20,531 --> 00:53:23,951
The lawyers are on their way
to the station.

938
00:53:24,994 --> 00:53:28,497
I will make sure they pay
for what they did to you.

939
00:53:30,416 --> 00:53:32,126
I'll sue everyone.

940
00:53:34,211 --> 00:53:35,379
It's fine.

941
00:53:36,339 --> 00:53:37,965
I don't want to make this a big deal.

942
00:53:38,049 --> 00:53:39,175
What?

943
00:53:40,134 --> 00:53:41,802
You'll let them get away with this?

944
00:53:42,970 --> 00:53:44,472
I don't want to see them again.

945
00:53:44,931 --> 00:53:47,308
No, no.
The lawyers will take care of that.

946
00:53:47,391 --> 00:53:48,643
Don't worry.

947
00:53:48,726 --> 00:53:50,019
But…

948
00:53:50,353 --> 00:53:53,814
if we sue them,
I'd be the talk of the town.

949
00:53:54,941 --> 00:53:57,568
I don't want to explain myself
over and over.

950
00:53:57,944 --> 00:53:59,320
And…

951
00:54:00,613 --> 00:54:03,783
I'd rather not worry Papa anymore.

952
00:54:04,241 --> 00:54:06,953
Can you not tell them what happened?

953
00:54:07,787 --> 00:54:08,788
What?

954
00:54:09,705 --> 00:54:11,999
You've been through so much,

955
00:54:12,959 --> 00:54:14,961
and you still worry about your father?

956
00:54:15,252 --> 00:54:17,171
I just don't want to be a burden.

957
00:54:17,505 --> 00:54:18,506
A burden?

958
00:54:20,257 --> 00:54:21,842
Is that what you think?

959
00:54:24,428 --> 00:54:25,429
Dear…

960
00:54:25,513 --> 00:54:27,348
you're not a burden.

961
00:54:28,099 --> 00:54:30,810
You almost got assaulted.

962
00:54:31,060 --> 00:54:33,187
Because you keep making deals with people

963
00:54:33,270 --> 00:54:35,272
you don't fully know.

964
00:54:35,356 --> 00:54:36,732
If Enzo and I didn't come in time,

965
00:54:36,816 --> 00:54:38,651
it would've been much worse.

966
00:54:38,734 --> 00:54:39,944
Do you understand?

967
00:54:40,027 --> 00:54:42,780
I didn't know that would happen!

968
00:54:42,863 --> 00:54:45,074
I've worked with that director
for a long time.

969
00:54:45,157 --> 00:54:46,951
-I thought…
-No, it's still wrong!

970
00:54:47,034 --> 00:54:49,286
It's still wrong to trust him
with everything!

971
00:54:49,370 --> 00:54:50,663
Remember that!

972
00:54:53,958 --> 00:54:54,959
I'm sorry.

973
00:54:55,042 --> 00:54:57,378
I'm sorry. I know it was my fault.

974
00:54:57,461 --> 00:54:58,671
I'm sorry for the bother.

975
00:54:58,754 --> 00:55:00,798
-I'm sorry, I was a burden to you.
-What burden?

976
00:55:02,383 --> 00:55:04,093
You're not a burden.

977
00:55:05,136 --> 00:55:07,221
You will never be a bother to me.

978
00:55:11,851 --> 00:55:13,185
You're right.

979
00:55:14,979 --> 00:55:16,272
I wasn't thinking.

980
00:55:18,315 --> 00:55:20,151
I'm such an idiot.

981
00:55:21,110 --> 00:55:23,320
Do you think I don't tell myself that?

982
00:55:23,404 --> 00:55:26,449
I'm stupid! I'm so stupid!
I'm such an idiot!

983
00:55:29,493 --> 00:55:31,579
You're not an idiot, dear.

984
00:55:31,662 --> 00:55:32,747
You're not.

985
00:55:36,208 --> 00:55:38,794
Mama's here. Mama's here, dear.

986
00:55:41,380 --> 00:55:42,381
Mama's here.

987
00:55:43,299 --> 00:55:44,925
It's done.

988
00:55:45,009 --> 00:55:46,802
It's okay, they're all gone.

989
00:55:46,886 --> 00:55:48,554
They're all gone now.

990
00:55:49,847 --> 00:55:51,265
They can't hurt you anymore.

991
00:55:51,849 --> 00:55:53,476
No more. No more.

992
00:55:55,102 --> 00:55:57,688
You're safe now. They're all gone.

993
00:56:04,487 --> 00:56:06,197
What if I wasn't able to save her?

994
00:56:06,280 --> 00:56:08,074
I would never forgive myself.

995
00:56:08,157 --> 00:56:10,284
Don't you want
to tell your family about it?

996
00:56:10,367 --> 00:56:11,786
It's not their problem to worry about.

997
00:56:11,869 --> 00:56:13,454
I just got fired.

998
00:56:13,537 --> 00:56:14,955
What do we do now?

999
00:56:15,039 --> 00:56:16,624
I am in charge of my life.

1000
00:56:16,707 --> 00:56:19,877
I get to decide what I want for myself.

1001
00:56:19,960 --> 00:56:22,838
I never do anything right
when it comes to her.

1002
00:56:22,922 --> 00:56:24,048
Is this your plan?

1003
00:56:24,131 --> 00:56:25,633
To be the next Mr. Aragon.

1004
00:56:25,716 --> 00:56:27,510
Diana loves La Familia more than her life.

1005
00:56:27,593 --> 00:56:30,805
What do you think
she would do to anyone who threatens it?
